WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.320
- I heard that actually-

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:02.400
Was it you two?

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:05.550
You play guitar and y'all kept
everybody entertained, right?

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:06.660
During the shoot?

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.940
- There was some music to be had

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:12.780
but mostly it was Jeff at the
piano and people joining him

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:13.920
'cause he can play anything,

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:15.690
and it was a lot of fun, a lot of fun.

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:17.701
- I like to play. He's a musical genius.

00:00:17.701 --> 00:00:18.840
(Chris scoffs)
There was a whole evening,

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:20.130
a one man show.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:21.480
If you give him a guitar...

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:22.560
- [Kelly] I had no idea.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:23.520
- Oh yeah. He's great.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.656
- I didn't know you played.

00:00:25.656 --> 00:00:27.840
- He sings. Just all kinds.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.501
- And you sing?
(Chris stammering)

00:00:29.501 --> 00:00:31.165
How did I miss this?

00:00:31.165 --> 00:00:34.565
- When Kelly Clarkson
asks you if you sing,

00:00:34.565 --> 00:00:36.599
you better be able to sing.

00:00:36.599 --> 00:00:37.565
(audience laughs)

00:00:37.565 --> 00:00:39.180
And I can't sing.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.820
- I'm just saying, it
could be a trio moment now,

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.460
'cause I didn't know he could do that too.

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:45.401
- He sings great.
(audience cheers)

00:00:45.401 --> 00:00:46.530
- I'm in.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:47.983
- He doesn't like to be fenced in either.

00:00:47.983 --> 00:00:49.800
- And DeWanda is a wonderful
singer. DeWanda sang with us.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.630
- Again, I echo what Chris just said,

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:53.241
when Kelly Clarkson asks

00:00:53.241 --> 00:00:55.050
if you can sing...
- Everyone is backing out.

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:57.450
Everyone is like, "I'm not
going karaoke-ing with you."

00:00:57.450 --> 00:00:59.760
It's not happening.
- I will. I'll karaoke.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.230
- I love karaoke.

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:03.690
Well, obviously, a whole
show I started with it.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:06.180
But I love it, 'cause
it's funny to do songs

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:08.490
people don't expect, so I usually rap.

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:09.690
What do you do at karaoke?

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:13.320
- Oh man, it kind of depends
on what I've been drinking

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:14.855
and how much I've been drinking, you know?

00:01:14.855 --> 00:01:18.270
- Yes. There is a difference
between beer and liquor.

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:20.400
- Yeah. I'm Whitney Houston
when I'm really drunk.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:21.233
- [Jeff] Wow.
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:21.233 --> 00:01:23.610
- But I'm "Pour Some Sugar On Me"

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:24.450
- I think we all are.
- when I'm just buzzed.

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.250
- Yes. Okay, okay.

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:27.750
What's your go-to for karaoke?

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:29.100
- I don't drink.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.403
- Well, you don't have to drink.

00:01:30.403 --> 00:01:31.433
(guests laughing)

00:01:31.433 --> 00:01:32.825
- That's a good answer.

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:35.070
- She's like, I don't drink,
therefore I don't do karaoke.

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:38.287
- Therefore, those two can't
exist without the other.

00:01:38.287 --> 00:01:39.372
- Correct, correct.
- That's amazing.

00:01:39.372 --> 00:01:43.553
- The last time I did
karaoke was with Amy Adams

00:01:43.553 --> 00:01:46.050
and I retired after that.

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:48.210
Have you ever done karaoke with her?

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:50.100
- No, but I've sung
with her in "Enchanted."

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.040
We sound great together at
home, when I'm singing with her.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.220
- She's serious about
karaoke. Very serious.

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:57.630
- She's got a great voice.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.900
- Yes. So I said I'm not
gonna take up anymore space

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:01.733
in the karaoke world.
- But people aren't supposed

00:02:01.733 --> 00:02:03.420
to be real at karaoke.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:05.280
You're supposed to be funny.

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:06.510
You're supposed to do some kind of funny-

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:07.560
if you really are a singer-

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.630
- She managed to do all of
those things simultaneously.

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:12.750
- Okay. Okay. Well, go ahead, Amy Adams,

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:15.348
be fabulous at everything.

00:02:15.348 --> 00:02:16.800
Do y'all like karaoke?

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.815
Well, you do it, you
probably sing everything.

00:02:19.815 --> 00:02:21.090
DeWanda, what's your go to?

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:24.930
- See, that's the thing. Bryce
and I are secretly twins.

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:28.624
So I also do not drink,
therefore I do not do karaoke.

00:02:28.624 --> 00:02:30.063
(DeWanda laughing)

00:02:30.063 --> 00:02:33.870
- We always learn about new
things every five minutes or so.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:35.520
- Every five minutes at least. Yeah.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:37.233
- We've never discussed
this prior to this moment.

00:02:37.233 --> 00:02:39.780
- This is news, but not news.
- Yes.

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:42.217
- Okay, what about you
Mamoudou? What do you do?

00:02:42.217 --> 00:02:44.437
- "Twist and Shout," I also
don't drink, by the way.

00:02:44.437 --> 00:02:45.300
"Twist and Shout."

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:46.707
- [Kelly] You don't drink either?

00:02:46.707 --> 00:02:47.813
- Nah. It's no good for me.

00:02:47.813 --> 00:02:50.550
- You don't have to drink,
it's an interesting thing.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:52.080
- Yeah, (indistinct)
some "Twist and Shout"

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:53.580
and "Sympathy for the Devil."

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:55.280
- [Kelly and DeWanda]
"Sympathy for the Devil."

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:56.830
♪ Please excuse me while I ♪

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:57.663
(Jeff sings gibberish)

00:02:57.663 --> 00:02:58.980
♪ I'm a man of wealth and taste ♪

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:00.379
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:00.379 --> 00:03:01.337
- Oh my God.

